feat(payments): move the single terminal into a register without re-typing its key

Corpusa is about to open its second counter, and the order of that
migration is a trap. The moment ANY register is enabled the tenant-level
SPIn block stops serving locations that have no register of their own —
it is not a fallback, it is superseded. So adding the new counter first
silently takes the ORIGINAL counter offline with
NO_REGISTER_FOR_LOCATION, at the point of sale.

The safe order is "register the terminal already in use FIRST", and by
hand that means re-typing an Auth Key the read path deliberately never
returns: one typo and the register is half-configured, which the
resolver also refuses. So the move happens server-side.

- settingsService.promoteSpinTerminalToRegister({ locationId, name }):
  appends a register carrying the legacy block's TPN, merchant number,
  callback and timeout, with the authKey CARRIED AS STORED BYTES
  (carrySettingSecret) — never decrypt→re-encrypt, the same rule
  blank-means-keep follows and for the same reason: one bad
  INTEGRATION_ENC_KEY read would erase a live credential instead of
  moving it. Refuses with words, never a 500, on: no complete terminal
  to move, no location, a location belonging to ANOTHER tenant (the
  cross-tenant form of the wrong-counter charge), and a TPN already
  registered (one device twice is gateway error 2005).
- The legacy block is LEFT INTACT on purpose: inert while any register
  is enabled, so disabling the new register rolls the tenant back to
  exactly its previous behaviour with no credential and no portal visit.
- POST /api/settings/payment-gateway/promote-terminal, ADMIN-gated and
  audited on the same trail as the save, metadata credential-free (a
  masked TPN and ids).
- Settings → Payment Gateway: the control appears inside the SPIn card
  only while the tenant HAS a complete terminal no register carries yet
  — mirroring the server's own ALREADY_PROMOTED guard so the button is
  never offered for a move the API would refuse. EN/ES.

Tests: terminal-registers 51/51, including the credential surviving the
move, the ORDERING case (after promoting, adding the second counter
leaves the first still charging on its own TPN), the documented rollback
(disable the register → TENANT_CONFIG governs again), and each refusal.
tenant-terminal 27/27, spin-tenant-config 7/7, terminal-select 4/4,
frontend 839/839 + next build clean. payment-capabilities and ipos-hpp
are red on this machine BEFORE this change too — not from here.

